{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.BringConeSplit","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.BringConeSplit","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Quaternion","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic","lean:module:QOU.BringCone"],"declarations":9,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Tetraplectic.Split.structure_constants","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Tetraplectic.Split.structure_constants","kind":"theorem","line":96,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BringConeSplit.lean#L96-L105","doc":"The structure constants of the two models, side by side: compact `(2, 2, 2)`, split\n`(2, −2, 2)`. Read as a Lie algebra on the imaginary units, the first is `𝔰𝔲(2)` and the\nsecond is `𝔰𝔩₂(R)`; a real rescaling of the basis cannot move between them. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Tetraplectic.Split.split_ne_compact","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Tetraplectic.Split.split_ne_compact","kind":"theorem","line":85,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BringConeSplit.lean#L85-L94","doc":"The flipped bracket is genuinely different from the compact one: at `p = 1` the split\n`[M_j, M_k]` is `−2i` while the compact `[M_j, M_k]` is `+2i`, and these differ whenever\n`4 ≠ 0` in `R`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Tetraplectic.Split.twist_ki","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Tetraplectic.Split.twist_ki","kind":"theorem","line":79,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BringConeSplit.lean#L79-L83","doc":"`[M_k, M_i] = 2 M_j`: the same as the compact model. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Tetraplectic.Split.twist_jk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Tetraplectic.Split.twist_jk","kind":"theorem","line":73,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BringConeSplit.lean#L73-L77","doc":"`[M_j, M_k] = −2 M_i`: the one sign that flips. In the compact model this is `+2 M_i`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Tetraplectic.Split.twist_ij","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Tetraplectic.Split.twist_ij","kind":"theorem","line":67,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BringConeSplit.lean#L67-L71","doc":"`[M_i, M_j] = 2 M_k`: the same as the compact model. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Tetraplectic.Split.M_k","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Tetraplectic.Split.M_k","kind":"def","line":63,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BringConeSplit.lean#L63-L65","doc":"Split Reeb operator `M_k` — right-multiplication by the hyperbolic unit `k = ij` (the\nrotated geodesic flow `X⊥`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Tetraplectic.Split.M_j","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Tetraplectic.Split.M_j","kind":"def","line":60,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BringConeSplit.lean#L60-L62","doc":"Split Reeb operator `M_j` — right-multiplication by the hyperbolic unit `j` (the geodesic\nflow `X`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Tetraplectic.Split.M_i","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Tetraplectic.Split.M_i","kind":"def","line":57,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BringConeSplit.lean#L57-L59","doc":"Split Reeb operator `M_i` — right-multiplication by the compact unit `i` (the fibre\nrotation `V`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Tetraplectic.Split.SplitBringCone","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Tetraplectic.Split.SplitBringCone","kind":"def","line":52,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BringConeSplit.lean#L52-L55","doc":"The split quaternions over `R`: `i² = −1`, `j² = +1`, `k = ij`, `k² = +1`. This is\n`M₂(R)`, with unit-norm elements `SL(2, R)` and imaginary part `𝔰𝔩₂(R)` — the algebra whose\nright-multiplication triad models the left-invariant frame of `PSL(2,ℝ)`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}